      "filename": "Statue of the Prince of Wales (later Edward VII), Temple Bar, London (4056362001).jpg",
      "title": "File:Statue of the Prince of Wales (later Edward VII), Temple Bar, London (4056362001).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/db/Statue_of_the_Prince_of_Wales_%28later_Edward_VII%29%2C_Temple_Bar%2C_London_%284056362001%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_the_Prince_of_Wales_(later_Edward_VII),_Temple_Bar,_London_(4056362001).jpg",
      "width": 2736,
      "height": 3648,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Elliott Brown from Birmingham, United Kingdom",
      "credit": "Temple Bar Memorial - Fleet Street, City of London - statue of the Prince of Wales (later King Edward VII)",
      "source": "Statue of the Prince of Wales (later Edward VII), Temple Bar, London (4056362001)",
      "description": "Buildings and monuments down Fleet Street in the City of London.\nThis is the current Temple Bar outside the Royal Courts of Justice, marking the boundary of the City of London with the City of Westminster.\nIt has a heraldic dragon on it.\nIt dates from 1880 on the site of a former gateway.\n(after the Sir Christopher Wren's Temple Bar was moved to Theobolds Park by Sir Henry Meux, where it remained until 2003, when it was dismantled stone by stone, so they could widen the road)\nThe stone monument has statues of Queen Victoria and the Prince of Wales (the later Edward VII - I thought that was him)\nI only got it from the Prince of Wales side (had no time to get the other side of it)\nI was wondering what \"Stood here\". Now I know, the Wren Temple Bar.\nIt is Grade II listed with a bronze griffin.\nTemple Bar Memorial - Heritage Gateway\nPrince Edward statue is by Joseph Boehm. Architect was Sir Horace Jones.\n\nPrince Edward, Prince of Wales - 1880",
      "dateCreated": "2009-10-17 12:26",
      "sourceType": "core",
      "sourceArticleId": "temple-bar-london-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "gcpv",
